# Annotated multi-round Chao-Reichardt weight-4 flag-gadget memory.
# Derived fixture (issue 146): the flagged-check schedule of
# flag_gadget_chao_reichardt_w4_multi_round.stim, unrolled for three rounds and
# completed into a memory experiment with DETECTOR and OBSERVABLE_INCLUDE
# annotations. Construction adapted from the published flagged-check schedule of
# Chao and Reichardt, arXiv:1912.09549; the annotations are authored for this
# audit, not taken from a published data file.
#
# Qubit roles: 0-3 data (reset to |0000>, measuring the ZZZZ stabilizer),
# 4 stabilizer ancilla, 5 flag ancilla. Every round's stabilizer (rec[-2]) and
# flag (rec[-1]) outcomes are deterministic without noise, so detectors compare
# consecutive rounds and the observable is the final Z_0 data measurement.
R 0 1 2 3 4 5
TICK
# Round 1
CX 0 4
TICK
CX 4 5
TICK
CX 1 4
TICK
CX 2 4
TICK
CX 4 5
TICK
CX 3 4
TICK
MR 4 5
TICK
DETECTOR rec[-2]
DETECTOR rec[-1]
# Round 2
CX 0 4
TICK
CX 4 5
TICK
CX 1 4
TICK
CX 2 4
TICK
CX 4 5
TICK
CX 3 4
TICK
MR 4 5
TICK
DETECTOR rec[-2] rec[-4]
DETECTOR rec[-1] rec[-3]
# Round 3
CX 0 4
TICK
CX 4 5
TICK
CX 1 4
TICK
CX 2 4
TICK
CX 4 5
TICK
CX 3 4
TICK
MR 4 5
TICK
DETECTOR rec[-2] rec[-4]
DETECTOR rec[-1] rec[-3]
M 0 1 2 3
OBSERVABLE_INCLUDE(0) rec[-4]
